para-dharmāt sv-anuṣṭhitāt
svabhāva-niyataṁ karma
kurvan nāpnoti kilbiṣam\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":4708,\"bb\":4121,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/18/47/b4121/\",\"shadow_value\":\"śreyān – better; sva-dharmaḥ – one’s own occupation; viguṇaḥ – imperfectly performed; para-dharmāt – than another’s occupation; su-anuṣṭhitāt – perfectly done; svabhāva-niyatam – prescribed according to one’s nature; karma – work; kurvan – performing; na – never; āpnoti – achieves; kilbiṣam – sinful reactions.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"śreyān\",\"translation\":\"better\"},{\"word\":\"sva-dharmaḥ\",\"translation\":\"one’s own occupation\"},{\"word\":\"viguṇaḥ\",\"translation\":\"imperfectly performed\"},{\"word\":\"para-dharmāt\",\"translation\":\"than another’s occupation\"},{\"word\":\"su-anuṣṭhitāt\",\"translation\":\"perfectly done\"},{\"word\":\"svabhāva-niyatam\",\"translation\":\"prescribed according to one’s nature\"},{\"word\":\"karma\",\"translation\":\"work\"},{\"word\":\"kurvan\",\"translation\":\"performing\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"never\"},{\"word\":\"āpnoti\",\"translation\":\"achieves\"},{\"word\":\"kilbiṣam\",\"translation\":\"sinful reactions\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":4709,\"bb\":4122,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/18/47/b4122/\",\"body_value\":\"It is better to engage in one’s own occupation, even though one may perform it imperfectly, than to accept another’s occupation and perform it perfectly. Duties prescribed according to one’s nature are never affected by sinful reactions.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":4710,\"bb\":4123,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/18/47/b4123/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"